.TH TEXT-EOL-NORMALIZE 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
text-eol-normalize \- safely inspect and normalize DOS CRLF line endings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B text-eol-normalize
.RI [ --check | --dry-run | --apply ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I FILE_OR_DIR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects selected text files for CRLF line endings. Defaults to read-only
inspection. Files already using LF are not rewritten. Requires explicit
.B --apply
to replace CRLF with LF. Mixed CRLF/LF is supported; standalone CR is skipped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check
Read-only inspection (default).
.TP
.B --dry-run
Report planned conversions without writing.
.TP
.B --apply
Allow replacement of eligible input files.
.TP
.B --recursive
Descend into subdirectories without following symbolic links.
.TP
.B --one-file-system
Do not cross device boundaries during recursive traversal.
.TP
.B --include EXT
Select extension; repeatable, overriding the default text allowlist.
.TP
.B --exclude EXT
Exclude extension; repeatable. bin and Excel formats are always excluded.
.TP
.B --min-age SECONDS
Skip files whose modification time is too recent.
.TP
.B --max-bytes N
Maximum permitted file size in bytes; default 16777216.
.TP
.B --verbose
Show skipped files and the reason.
.TP
.B --help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Show command and version, then exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B text-eol-normalize --check --recursive /srv/import
Find candidate files; no writes.
.TP
.B text-eol-normalize --apply --recursive --min-age 120 /srv/import
Convert established files in an import staging directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: successful operation (even if DOS files were found).
1: file processing errors.
2: invalid arguments.
.SH SAFETY
No write unless --apply is provided. Symlinks, hardlinks, setuid/setgid
files, unsupported encodings, binary data and standalone CR text are skipped.
Only current-user-owned files are replaced. Conversion uses a private staging
file and same-directory rename. Inodes and timestamps change; ACLs, extended
attributes, special flags and sparse layout are not preserved. Concurrent
noncooperating writers are not protected by the rename operation. Use completed
files in a controlled staging directory and an external cooperative scheduler
lock. No fsync durability guarantee is provided.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dos2unix (1),
.BR crontab (5),
.BR flock (1)
